From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Heikki Krogerus <heikki.krogerus@linux.intel.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:54:40 +0530
Subject: i2c: designware: Don't warn about missing
 get_clk_rate_khz

The Intel Xe I2C controller has no functional input clock, so
dev->get_clk_rate_khz is never set. i2c_dw_set_timings_master() still calls
i2c_dw_clk_rate() to compute the SCL HCNT/LCNT values, which triggered a
WARN_ON_ONCE() splat on every xe module load once the controller started
probing in polling mode:

  WARNING: CPU: 14 PID: 1830 at drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c:474 i2c_dw_clk_rate+0x10/0x20
   i2c_dw_probe_master+0xfd/0x5c0
   dw_i2c_plat_probe+0x32f/0x3d0
   xe_i2c_probe+0x1b9/0x350 [xe]

Running without an input clock is a legitimate configuration (the bus speed
comes from the "clock-frequency" property). Downgrade the WARN to a
dev_dbg_once() and return 0, matching upstream.

Signed-off-by: Heikki Krogerus <heikki.krogerus@linux.intel.com>
Acked-by: Jarkko Nikula <jarkko.nikula@linux.intel.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20250513124015.2568924-1-heikki.krogerus@linux.intel.com
(cherry-pick from bdf4442f4c7e8feb0733ee4de4d4ff7aa8b1c11d)
Signed-off-by: Nitin Gote <nitin.r.gote@intel.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c
index 5e7665e293bd..efd1b997bce8 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c
@@ -504,8 +504,10 @@ u32 i2c_dw_clk_rate(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)
 	 * Clock is not necessary if we got LCNT/HCNT values directly from
 	 * the platform code.
 	 */
-	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(!dev->get_clk_rate_khz))
+	if (!dev->get_clk_rate_khz) {
+		dev_dbg_once(dev->dev, "Callback get_clk_rate_khz() is not defined\n");
 		return 0;
+	}
 	return dev->get_clk_rate_khz(dev);
 }
 
